`3e01023` (source, build.py) and `0d804bc` (`generated/` repinned). This repo
had written the opposite of the drift rule into its bundler ("THIS LIST IS A
DELIBERATE COPY and the drift is accepted"), reasoning about coupling to a
SIBLING's bundler; `compiler-order.txt` is upstream's own file, so the list is
derived now like the other two, and the header says why. The harness takes
`compile-frontend-ir` -> `prepare-method-ir` and hands the prepared chapter
straight to `emit-wasm-chapter-stream`: no IR text, so the 945 MB round trip
