### Roc: the timer builtins, and why they reached Roc at all

rust-codex-compiler `6255747`: rocemit and codexrun give `pit-input-hz` 1193182
and `pit-count` 11932 (x86's constant helpers, X86_64Boot.codex) and
`cpu-park` 0 (`sti; hlt`, answering 0). roc-apps `8513cd2`: ladder **740 ->
753 PASS**, 253 -> 239 REFUSED; `cpu-park`'s own test times the halt against
the HPET and is DIVERGES (its `answers 0 0` line is language, and passes).
Sweep 743 -> 744.

Steve asked how a PIT constant reached Roc, machine code being out of scope.
It did not reach the programs: `fat32-parse` cites GopFat16 -> GopDisk ->
GopUsbMsc/GopXhci, and U62 rewrote GopXhci's `xhci-ms-ticks` onto the exact
PIT constants. **rocemit emits every cited chapter whole** (one module per
chapter), so one definition no program calls refused the unit.

**The same holds for the list-parameter refusal U62 widened.** In five of its
33 regressions sampled (e1000-aneg-budget, e1000-asde-arms, dhcp-acquire,
net-drain-budget, forewords@encode-qoi) the refused definition
(`e1000-copy-into`, `ne2k-copy-into`, `qoi-decode-pixels`) is in the unit but
absent from upstream's own IR, which every upstream backend prunes to what
`opening` and the declared exports reach before emitting. Pruning rocemit's
input the same way would clear those without teaching the emitter the shape.
That changes rocemit's "whole chapter" output design: Steve's call.

### rocemit prunes like upstream (Steve's call)

rust-codex-compiler `8937ef5`, roc-apps `0886f90`. rocemit emitted every
cited chapter whole; it now prunes the lowered definitions to what
`ir-emit-roots` reaches (the crate's own `prune_unreachable_roots` and
`IR_EMIT_ROOTS`), as every upstream backend does. A unit with no `opening`
stays whole. Every `__eq_<T>` is a root too: upstream's lowering names the
instantiated helper, ours lowers `==` to a Binary node that roc_emit resolves
by name, and without them ten passing units lost equality in Roc.

    ladder   753 -> 836 PASS, 239 -> 153 REFUSED, 18 DIVERGES (+net-ack-leak,
             a __heap-save measurement), no pass lost

The whole-chapter design served one caller, canvas_apps/safari/emitted.sh,
retired 2026-09-18 (safari's Roc is source now); no `--whole` flag was kept.
Not run here: roc-apps floor/ (`--by-reach`), which this also prunes.

**CORRECTION: it had a second caller, roc-apps tests/package.py**, which
builds tests/ported/ by taking each chapter's text from the FIRST unit that
emits it and sharing it with every test. That is sound only if a chapter's
text does not depend on the program, and pruning made it depend on the
program. package.py runs every app before keeping it, so it would drop tests
silently, not ship broken ones. Fixed below (`rocemit --whole`).

