### roc-apps tests/ported: emitted whole, with crash stubs (Steve's call)

    rust-codex-compiler 0322b24, roc-apps aa02052
    ported   521 -> 566 tests; every packaged app runs with no Roc error

`rocemit --whole` writes every definition of every chapter, unpruned, and
package.py uses it. A function rocemit cannot write becomes
`|_, ...| crash("rocemit could not write ...")`; a constant is left out.
Probed on the nightly first: an unreached function stub compiles clean and a
reached one crashes with its message, but a `crash` in a top-level constant
is a build error even unused, because Roc evaluates constants while it
compiles. Dependents follow (a function using something left out is stubbed,
a constant is left out, and so is a constant that could reach a stub), as
does a lifted lambda whose users are gone. rocemit prints each on stderr;
package.py keeps them in gen/whole/<unit>/notes.txt.

What was left out across all ~850 whole emissions: proof claims (propeq and
`proof` types, no runtime meaning); four effectful constants (`current-user`,
`authenticate`, `key-public`, `respond-not-found`); class dictionaries with
no Roc type (UNSUPPORTED_FREE_BINDER) and the lambdas lifted out of them; and
`fe-sqrt-m1`, which can reach the list-parameter stub `fe-carry-pass`. No
machine constants: those are no longer hand-kept at all.

**Constant builtins come from upstream.** `builtins_probe.py
--rust-constants` reads the builtins x86 emits as constants
(`emit-constant-helper st "<name>" <ident>` and `<ident> : Integer = N`, in
Emit/) and prints CONSTANT_BUILTINS, which the interpreter and rocemit answer
from. At U62: pit-input-hz 1193182, pit-count 11932. `cpu-park` is a routine
and stays hand-kept (0).

Whole mode also exposed `__compare_Boolean`/`__compare_Real` lowered through
Integer temporaries (upstream's gen-int-compare, normally pruned); rocemit
writes them in Roc directly.

### Roc: list-parameter writes (in progress, off by default)

rust-codex-compiler `src/list_versions.rs`, behind `rocemit --list-versions`;
status and next steps in its `docs/list-versions.md`. Codex writes a list in
place; the pass makes each write a new version, has a function that writes a
list parameter hand the last version back (as its answer, or as a tuple),
and has callers continue with it. On the 35 units refused at U62 for "writes
its list parameter": 24 PASS, 8 correctly REFUSED (a write to a list held in
a record field, which is shared heap), 2 FAIL (lib@brotli-test's sizes;
e1000-rx-reuse, a heap measurement), 1 CRASH (lib@brotli-dict-test). Not the
default until Brotli is understood and the full ladder shows no PASS lost.
The default path is unchanged (full ladder re-run to confirm).
